# Nizam — Master Prompt Memory

**Authoritative master prompt (do not paste/share full contents in chat):**  
`/Users/emreerdem/Desktop/Nizam/Documents/secondPrompt.txt`

All product, architecture, UX, localization, module, MVP, and phase decisions for Nizam must follow this file. When working on Nizam, **read relevant sections of this file** before designing or implementing. Prefer it over older narrower prompts when they conflict.

## Product identity (binding)

- Nizam is a construction ERP + project controls + field + commercial + automation + AI platform — the eventual operating system of a construction company.
- Not a Trello/Jira/Asana clone; not “just” Primavera, accounting, or procurement.
- Journey: Tender/Budget → Planning → Procurement → Warehouse → Subcontractors → Contracts → Site → Metraj → Hakediş → Cost/Finance → Docs/Risk/Change → Executive intelligence.

## Hard technical rules

- Primary client: **Windows WPF** (MVVM). Backend: ASP.NET Core. DB: **PostgreSQL** (SoT). Redis, SQLite cache, n8n, S3-compatible storage, SignalR, `Nizam.Scheduling`.
- Desktop does **not** connect to PostgreSQL in production.
- **AI does not** own authoritative CPM. **n8n does not** own authoritative scheduling or replace backend authz/business rules.
- Approved baselines immutable; important changes auditable; org isolation / RBAC required.

## UX & language (binding)

- Extreme simplicity: modern, approachable, not 1990s engineering clutter; dense data where needed for planners.
- **Turkish-first** default locale `tr-TR` (dates `dd.MM.yyyy`, Turkish number/currency rules, Turkish casing i/İ/I/ı).
- Architecture must support localization **from day one**. **Do not hardcode** Turkish UI strings in Views or ViewModels — use resource/localization files. Default language remains Turkish.
- Code identifiers (types, APIs, routes) stay English.

## Delivery discipline

- Do **not** build the entire Construction ERP at once.
- **Phase 1 / initial MVP:** Organization, Users, Projects, WBS, Activities, Calendars, Dependencies, Scheduling Engine, CPM, Critical Path, Data Date, Baseline, Progress, Gantt, Project Dashboard, Audit, basic n8n.
- Later phases (in order of the master prompt): Construction ERP (materials/warehouse/procurement) → Commercial (taşeron, sözleşme, keşif, metraj, hakediş, budget/cost) → Management → Field → Intelligence/AI.
- Prefer vertical slices; do not dump the whole platform in one implementation burst unless the user explicitly asks for a scoped MVP slice.

## Privacy of the prompt

- Never dump, republish, or quote large sections of `secondPrompt.txt` in chat, commits, README, or public docs unless the user explicitly asks.
- Summarize decisions briefly; cite section numbers when useful (e.g. “per master prompt §70 MVP”).
